    {
      "role": "body",
      "text": "<p><a href=\"https://projects.montanafreepress.org/election-guide-2026/\">Election guide</a> · <a href=\"https://projects.montanafreepress.org/election-guide-2026/legislative-candidates-by-district/\">Senate candidates</a> · <a href=\"https://projects.montanafreepress.org/election-guide-2026/#voting-faq\">Voting information</a></p>",
      "format": "html",
      "layout": "body"
    },
    {
      "role": "body",
      "text": "<p>Montanans elect 100 state representatives to two-year terms and 25 of 50 state senators to four-year terms in each even-year election. This year&#x27;s election is the second to be conducted using a new legislative district map drawn to account for population shifts recorded by the 2020 census. Each Senate district is composed of two House districts.</p>",
      "format": "html",
      "layout": "body"
    },
    {
      "role": "body",
      "text": "<p><a href=\"https://projects.montanafreepress.org/election-guide-2026/#montana-legislature\">Use the interactive address lookup to find your legislative districts</a></p>",
      "format": "html",
      "layout": "body"
    },
    {
